1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,890
Reading a poem about seasons Millie is reading a poem about the seasons of the year.

2
00:00:09,890 --> 00:00:12,585
Here is the poem.

3
00:00:12,585 --> 00:00:27,310
Seasons of the year Winter days are full of snow, when trees and flowers forget to grow, and the birds fly far away, to find a warm and sunny day.

4
00:00:27,310 --> 00:00:33,440
The days of spring are windy and bright, a perfect time to fly a kite.

5
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:39,450
Bees and butterflies play among flowers, then hide from April showers.

6
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:52,690
Those sweet memories of summer days are about quiet streams and trees and shade, lazy afternoons by a pool, and eating ice-cream to feel cool.

7
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:59,650
Then autumn leaves turn brown, fall into piles upon the ground.

8
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:06,580
Farmers work to harvest crops, as the days get shorter and the temperature drops.

9
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:12,840
Soon the snowy season will begin, and it will be a new year once again.
